    {
      "id": "529251dc0e828109d8dfd96811974136a8c9f86f",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 703603733,
          "type": null,
          "body": "The Windows builds are failing, e.g. https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/jobs/1678992639, with the error\n\n```\nError copying file (if different) from \"C:/gitlab-builds/builds/-fyeYoMP/0/wireshark/wireshark/build/doc/androiddump.html\" to \"C:/gitlab-builds/builds/-fyeYoMP/0/wireshark/wireshark/build/run/RelWithDebInfo/androiddump.html\".\n```\n\n(There were similar errors in the macOS builds, which I fixed in !4619 and !4620; I'd try to fix the Windows one, but, at least on my W10 VM, I can't seem to install a JRE/Asciidoctorj combination where CMake can find Asciidoctor, I just get\n\n```\n-- Could NOT find Asciidoctor: Found unsuitable version \"JAVA_HOME\", but required is at least \"1.5\" (found C:/ProgramData/chocolatey/bin/asciidoctorj.exe)\n```\n\nI tried both `choco install javaruntime` and `choco install openjdk`, combined with `choco install -y asciidoctorj xsltproc docbook-bundle`.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-10-14T10:06:40.571Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-10-14T10:06:40.571Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 121176327,
